  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- The track labeled unknown is 'How Could I Know?', later called 'Oxen' at the 28 May 2004 Toronto show, avoiding confusion with another title [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2004-01-31dpa4021.flac24** (recommended): source not stated; 15 songs; 103 min; rated 4.5/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Uploader warns the 24-bit files must not be bit-depth converted or resampled, and will not burn to audio CD [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The unknown song is rumored to appear on the band's next studio album; it was named 'Oxen' at Toronto on 28 May 2004 [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2004-01-31dpa4021.flac24**: taped by Matt DeNardo; transferred by Matt DeNardo; source: DPA 4021s (XY) > Grace Lunatec V3 > AES > Metric Halo Mobile I/O ULN-2 clocked to V3 > Firewire > Powerbook G3 400 Pismo running OS 10.3 > Metric Halo beta… [1]. Also: Source compiled on 11 February 2004 by Matt DeNardo, from a 24-bit recording that cannot be burned to audio CD [1]",
